        "status": "DISCHARGED",
        "justification": "Each of 18 bridge choices uses two distinct short neighbors of the third retained hole u, then all short perfect matchings of the remaining required vertices. Enumerating the least remaining vertex is complete without duplication. Repeated original edges and cyclic components are rejected."
      },
      {
        "id": "MC8",
        "claim": "Duplicate endpoint stubs and isolated vertices",
        "status": "DISCHARGED",
        "justification": "The endpoint list has c+4 distinct stub positions, although the underlying A label can repeat. If a J endpoint is an original port, it is isolated in F_A union N and pairs its crossing stub to its bridge stub; expansion restores this single A vertex. A bridge coinciding with an original crossing yields two parallel compressed edges and is rejected as a two-cycle."
      },
      {
        "id": "MC9",
        "claim": "Compression and positive transfer",
        "status": "DISCHARGED",
        "justification": "After an accepted forest is attached, all ten terminal B vertices have degree one, all retained interior vertices degree two, and free 0_B degree zero. Acyclicity gives exactly five paths. Their matching is tested in the correct 11-cycle table. Expanding adds 15 A vertices and 4 removed B vertices, giving 30 distinct vertices, all 13 original edges, and only short other edges."
      },
      {
        "id": "MC10",
        "claim": "Finite fourbridge input coverage",
        "status": "DISCHARGED",
        "justification": "A generation count is binomial(12,c)*(11-c)!!; every residual B input is checked with every one of c! orders of its sorted ports. All spectra may select their own bridge choice, forest and positive table entry. Exact residual byte streams, premature EOF and trailing bytes were checked by the independent adjacency/component implementation."
      },
      {
